WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.320
<v Instructor>So now let's talk</v>

2
00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:03.780
about CloudWatch Network Synthetic Monitor.

3
00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:06.900
So the idea is that you have connected your cloud

4
00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.020
to your on-premises corporate data center

5
00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:12.870
through Direct Connect or a VPN connection,

6
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.700
and you want to detect network issues

7
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.120
between your data center and AWS.

8
00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:21.270
That is precisely what this Network Synthetic Monitor

9
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:22.320
is doing.

10
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:23.490
So you're going to identify

11
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:25.920
any type of network performance degradation,

12
00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.410
such as packet loss, latency, or jitter.

13
00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.630
You don't need to install any agents.

14
00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:33.510
It will test ICMP or TCP traffic

15
00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.900
on IPv4 on-premises traffic

16
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:38.160
through your Direct Connect

17
00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:40.380
or your site-to-site VPN connection.

18
00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.260
So all the metrics and the results are going to be published

19
00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.930
to CloudWatch Metrics so you can take proper action.

20
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:48.690
The idea is that it's a way for you to ensure

21
00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.670
that the connection you established

22
00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.300
between your data center and AWS is working as expected

23
00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:56.790
and you get that information in real time.

24
00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:58.590
So that's it. I hope you liked it.

25
00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:00.693
And I will see you in the next lecture.

